<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qavurt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1073">1073</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Kavurt, Qara Arslan Beg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qavurt was a Seljuk prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaghri-beg">Chaghri Beg</a> and elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan">Alp Arslan</a>, who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> in the 1040s and founded the Seljuk dynasty there. He extended his rule to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> across the Gulf. After Alp Arslan's death he claimed the sultanate, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-shah-i">Malik Shah</a> defeated him near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a> in 1073 and had him killed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qavurt.jpg" alt="Qavurt" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LouisAragon (uploader) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Ahmad_Qavurt,_minted_in_Jiroft.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
